<section id="about" class="about">
  <p class="section-label">About</p>
  <div class="prose about-prose">
    <p>
I'm a software engineer who works across different levels of a system, 
from embedded systems to mobile applications, SDKs, and backend services. 
I like to understand the broader system and the goals behind a project, then make technical decisions that support those goals.
    </p>
    <p>
Throughout my career, I have worked across these different layers, 
from building embedded products and their companion applications to developing an iOS SDK for the automotive industry. 
My work extends beyond implementation: I contribute to architecture and API design, document systems, and capture the reasoning behind 
technical decisions throughout a project's lifecycle.
    </p>
    <p>
In my free time, I build projects to explore technologies and ideas. 
Through NC-750, I experiment with how privacy-oriented and user-controlled software can be designed. Its first application, Mirror, 
grew from that exploration into a shipped AI-assisted application that uses LLMs to guide users through a structured interview and generate a portable 
personal profile. 
It supports both local and hosted AI providers, with an emphasis on keeping users in control of their data and provider choices.
    </p>
    <p>
        Outside of technical work, my time goes to my homelab, music, video games, cinema, and discovering new things and cultures.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

